## Source tree vs. deployment

An earlier version of this file said the repository "does not redistribute
text-to-speech voice model files". That is true of the **git tree**, and
false of a **deployment**:

- The Supertonic weights are not tracked here. The `supertonic` package
  downloads them into a cache directory (`SUPERTONIC_CACHE_DIR`, default
  `~/.cache/supertonic3`) on first use — see `supertonic-service/README.md`.
- A deployment that ships that cache preloaded — a prebuilt filesystem image,
  a copied cache directory, a container layered on top of it — therefore
  redistributes the weights.
- Voice style files are gitignored (§Voice files), but any the deployment
  installs into its style directory travel with it.

Anyone distributing a deployment is responsible for the obligations of the
licenses below — not merely for what this repository tracks.

